WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:18.640
Shall we go to Dubai or to Riyadh? That is a crucial question occupying the minds of CEOs and other boards of directors,

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.720
in some of the world's largest companies today, that want to have regional headquarters in the Middle East and North Africa

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.960
in order to oversee and manage their business and operations here in the region.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.960
Until recently, this question was not being asked.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:38.000
Simply because any international company that was thinking of implementing a regional headquarter here in the region

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.680
would undoubtedly choose Dubai.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:46.440
For two reasons.. The first is that Dubai, as one of the most successful global cities,

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:53.000
provides almost all the advantages and facilities that any international company might dream of or need

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.280
in order to launch its operations all over the countries of the region through it.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.200
For example, we will find international companies established in countries such as Egypt, Saudi Arabia, Tunisia, Algeria

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.240
and others, but they are managed from the Dubai International Financial Center

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:10.160
or Dubai Internet City through the regional headquarters of those companies there.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:18.040
The second reason is that in reality, for many years, there was no real and strong competitor in the region for Dubai

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:22.600
that is keen to offer the same advantages that the Emirati city offers

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.680
to multinational companies interested in being present in the region.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:35.320
In Europe, there are Zurich, Frankfurt, London, Paris, Amsterdam and Geneva all vying for regional corporate headquarters.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.840
In Asia there are Hong Kong, Singapore, Tokyo, Shanghai, Beijing, Shenzhen and Seoul.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:46.880
In North America there are New York, San Francisco, Los Angeles, Boston, Washington, Chicago and Toronto.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:50.120
Here in the region, there is virtually no other than Dubai.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.840
I know that there are international companies with regional headquarters in Cairo, Riyadh,

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.680
Abu Dhabi, Manama and Casablanca, but all these cities combined

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.000
do not have half the number of regional headquarters located in Dubai.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:06.720
This is the current situation, but it seems that Dubai will not remain the only player.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.920
This is simply because Saudi Arabia for the first time started to put this in mind.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:17.320
During the last two years, the Kingdom's keenness to make Riyadh

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.040
the economic capital and the most important financial center in the region was clearly evident.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.320
This is the title that Dubai currently enjoys.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:30.120
The bottom line is that the Saudi efforts in this direction are so serious that we are now watching mega international companies

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.800
moving their regional headquarters from Dubai to Riyadh, as we will explain later.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.240
Other companies that are still new to the region are going directly to Riyadh, not to Dubai.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.200
In short, there is an economic boom currently taking place in the heart of Riyadh for the first time.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.680
This situation really makes us ask some serious questions, including:

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.320
Why are companies confused in choosing between Dubai and Riyadh?

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.200
What might Riyadh offer to make international companies

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.360
that want to establish headquarters in the region choose them instead of Dubai?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.720
Is there a precise Saudi plan to achieve this?

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:08.000
Can we consider Riyadh's efforts as direct competition with Dubai? Will Dubai stand idly by?

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.840
Are we in the midst of a fierce competition between the two cities,

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:14.000
as is the fierce competition between Singapore and Hong Kong?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.280
The most important question is, why this competition over this issue in the first place?

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.320
What is the gain for any country if it attracts a large number of regional headquarters of international companies to its lands?

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:27.069
This is a sampling of the significant questions we'll be discussing in today's episode.

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:33.480
But before that, I want to remind you that half of those who are watching us until today are still not subscribed to the channel.

