00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:53.920
In the early eighties, East Asian countries such as China and Japan, and Asian tigers such as South Korea, Taiwan, Hong Kong

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:57.200
and Singapore, were able to achieve giant economic successes.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.960
The most notable feature of these successes is that they were not based on neither the socialist model,

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:07.360
nor the traditional Western capitalist model based on the free market without state intervention.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:14.080
Because, unlike the socialist model, those Asian countries did not fully control the economy,

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:20.800
on the contrary, they gave the private sector large free space. On the other hand, unlike the free capitalist model,

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:25.520
these governments did not let the economy or development paths run completely free.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.360
That is, they did not absolutely let the rules of the free market lead the country.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.520
Well, what were they doing?

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:36.360
The approach taken by these countries can be considered a combination between socialist and capitalist

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:42.960
[half socialist, half capitalist] rules. Briefly, the governments of those countries had certain development agendas.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.920
It wanted to achieve goals in certain development sectors. To do so,

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:52.800
it intervened in the economy by guiding the private sector and helping it achieve that agenda.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:59.320
For example, in the case of the giant electronic chip industry in Taiwan, which is considered the most advanced in the world.

00:05:59.320 --> 00:06:04.720
The one that drew up the plan in the eighties, saved resources and decided to take the country towards this path,

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:08.360
is the Taiwanese government itself. Yet, the one that implemented the plan at the time

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.440
and that owns the same industry today is the private sector.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:17.600
Consequently, terms such as the “capitalist developmental state” -

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.440
the “state-sponsored capitalism” -

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.920
and the “guided capitalism” popped up since then.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:30.080
In fact, this is the closest pattern to the path that the UAE city of Dubai has followed in its development plan.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:37.000
You can say that all of Dubai's successes are the result of initiatives launched by the government in the city,

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.280
with the participation of the private sector itself in their implementation and success later.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:45.480
We can say that those responsible for planning for Dubai had their eyes on Singapore all along.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.760
That's why Singapore and Dubai are very similar in so many ways.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:58.680
In this context, Dubai decided to invest its revenues from oil, which are few compared to the revenues of Abu Dhabi,

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:03.320
by the way, in developing economic activities that could generate great income for it in the future

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:08.520
in order to build a developed and sustainable economy, and the intention was to develop a service economy.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:13.920
Here the regime in Dubai made an amazing shift in economic development that is rarely repeated..

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:19.760
The natural path of development that most developed countries followed was through the transition from agriculture

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:23.760
to non-agricultural activities, or from industry to a service economy.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.520
But in Dubai, the shift has been from an economy based on trade and pearl fishing,

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:31.960
to an economy based on services directly, like Singapore,

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:41.560
whose service sector employs more than 84% of its workforce, and is responsible for more than 70% of GDP.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:47.240
But, in order to create a developed service economy in a city like Dubai, in the way it was in the seventies,

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:54.240
a great change needed to be done. Government officials in Dubai put a lot of money into infrastructure projects:

00:07:54.240 --> 00:08:00.120
roads, ports, airports, and the development and improvement of public services such as electricity, water,

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:06.800
and telecommunications. But all this, despite its importance, is not enough to make the city the focus of attention for

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:11.200
international companies that might be interested in being present in the Middle East.

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:16.160
That is why Dubai has made laws, institutional frameworks, legislation and regulatory rules

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:22.520
that govern the rules of work in the city and make things easier for companies and for any visitor to the city above all.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:27.400
At the same time, it provided tax and customs privileges for companies, and not only that.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:33.720
The government also launched important strategic projects such as Dubai Internet City, Dubai Media City,

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:40.960
Dubai International Financial Center, and Dubai World Trade Center, other than free trade zones and tourism projects.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:46.960
All of this was eventually translated into the fact that today's Dubai has become one of the most important cities in the world.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:51.600
The most important and largest financial center in the Middle East and North Africa.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:56.360
The place where most of the regional headquarters of international companies

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:58.360
in the region and even the media reside.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:03.320
This is natural, given that Dubai provides companies and individuals

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:09.400
with almost all the facilities and services that they can obtain in large global cities such as New York and London.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:15.720
What is not normal is that our region, for a long time, has had no other city like Dubai.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.160
There is no strong competitor to the city, an important note,

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:24.920
which is that the closest competitor to Dubai as a financial center is its peer Abu Dhabi, i.e the Emirates as well.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:29.800
The absence of competition has had a direct result of the concentration of most of the regional headquarters

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:33.600
of international companies in Dubai, regardless of the markets they target.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:40.000
I.e, One can find a company whose main market is the Egyptian market, yet its regional headquarters are in Dubai, not Cairo.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.440
A TV channel targeting the Saudi audience, based in Dubai, not Riyadh.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:49.600
An institution targeting the Algerian market based in Dubai, not Algeria, and so on..

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:54.080
In fact, this is a skill on the part of the Emiratis who were able to provide the environment and conditions

00:09:54.080 --> 00:10:00.720
that convinced international and even Arab companies to take Dubai as a starting point for their operations and activities

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:05.520
in the region, regardless of the country or countries targeted by these economic activities.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:13.080
The whole region has reconciled with this situation ever since, but in the last two years it has been pretty clear

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:17.520
that officials in Saudi Arabia have a different plan whose goal, in short,

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:25.520
is to make the capital, Riyadh, the most important city in the region financially, economically and commercially.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.000
It is the title that Dubai currently enjoys, as we said in the first episode.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:34.560
Let us look at the global ranking of Arab capitals in the list of the largest financial centers in the world.

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:38.080
We will find Dubai first in the Arab world and 17th in the world.

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:44.000
Then Abu Dhabi ranked 32, then Casablanca ranked 54th,

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:51.440
then Doha ranked 57, then Bahrain ranked 81, then Riyadh ranked 98,

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:56.600
and finally, Kuwait which is ranked 108th in the list of the most important financial centers in the world.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:11:00.000
Riyadh does not like its arrangement. It wants to be number one,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.680
and this is an ambitious project based on the fact that the capital of the country

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.240
has the richest and largest economy in the region.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:10.680
Perhaps the most significant desire of the Saudis is that

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:16.840
they want to achieve their goal much faster than the time needed by Dubai to reach its current position.

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:22.760
In order to achieve this, the Saudis decided to use two different methods in parallel and at the same time

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:26.040
within the principle of "carrot-and-stick", so to speak.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:33.640
The first method, "the stick", is the difficult method in which the financial and economic weight of the Saudi state is exploited.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:43.040
The second method, "the carrot", is the soft one through which all the privileges and facilities that international companies

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:48.200
meight need to open their regional headquarters in Riyadh are provided [which they are already enjoying in Dubai].

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:52.200
Ok, one may wonder how this happens on the ground?

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:52.960
Well, that is how…

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:57.560
In February 2021, Saudi Finance Minister Mohammed Abdullah Al-Jadaan

00:11:57.560 --> 00:12:03.520
made a surprising and interesting statement to Reuters. He said that the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia,

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:07.920
which is the largest economy in the region and the largest exporter of oil all over the world,

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:12.200
will completely stop awarding any government contracts to international companies

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:18.840
that have a regional headquarters in the region outside Riyadh, and this will be implemented starting from 2024.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:23.320
The words of the Saudi officials to international companies were simply and briefly as follows:

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:31.120
You want to obtain contracts for mega projects whose value reaches billions of dollars and sometimes tens of billions?

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.560
You have to establish your regional headquarters in Riyadh, not in any other city in the region.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:43.360
You are free: take it or leave it. But starting from January 1, 2024, and this is still by the lips of the Saudi officials,

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:47.560
no company will get even a single contract from the government.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:52.000
Of course, you can work with the Saudi private sector freely, as you know.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.560
But acquiring government contracts without your headquarters inside Riyadh! It won't happen.

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:59.840
The Saudi minister, explaining the reasons for this sudden decision, told Reuters:

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:05.320
We cannot be the owners of the largest economy in the region, and at the same time, Saudi Arabia's share of

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:09.680
the regional headquarters of international companies located in the region is only 5%.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:14.200
Other than that, we want to attract more international companies to invest in Saudi Arabia.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.680
On the one hand we provide job opportunities for Saudis.

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:21.160
On the other hand, we diversify our economy and make it less dependent on oil.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:26.520
The most prominent feature of the Saudi decision announced by Al-Jadaan was not being a bold decision only,

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:32.280
but in fact it is a big bet on the part of the Saudis using their financial and strategic influence.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:37.040
A bet from their side on the great economic importance of their country for international companies,

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:42.400
which are supposed to be interested in preserving their great interests and business with the Kingdom’s government,

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:47.720
and for this you will see that it is in their interest that their regional headquarters be located in Riyadh.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:53.480
Since it is a bet like any other bet in the world, the Saudis may win or lose.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:57.400
There is about a year left until the end of the government's deadline for international companies,

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:02.760
but from the time the decision was announced until now, it seems, and God knows best, that it is a winning bet.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:03.640
How is that?

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.720
Attention please…

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:11.560
In October of the same year, Al-Jadaan’s statement, 2021, and during the “Future Investment Initiative” activities

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:15.920
held in Riyadh under the supervision of the Saudi Public Investment Fund,

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:19.880
44 international companies obtained licenses

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:24.400
allowing them to establish their regional headquarters in the region in the Saudi capital.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:33.520
These companies included big names such as PepsiCo, Pricewaterhouse, KPMG, Deloitte, Unilever, Samsung, Siemens,

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:39.640
Dimension Data, Tim Hortons, Halliburton, Philips, Novartis, Johnson Controls, and Schlumberger.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:44.880
And “500 Startups”, “Baker Hughes” - “Eli Lilly” -“SAP” - Medtronic, and others.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:50.400
Almost half of the companies that obtained these licenses had already signed agreements

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:56.000
to transfer their regional headquarters to Riyadh months before, specifically in January 2021.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.760
The other half were new companies negotiating with them for the first time

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:03.240
over the establishing their regional headquarters in Riyadh.

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:08.560
By the way, the Saudis do not want a large number of companies without considering their economic weight,

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:13.720
on the contrary, they only target companies whose annual revenues exceed one billion dollars.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.000
Here an important question arises: What are the motives of those companies? Or,

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:23.000
more precisely, what drives them to establish their regional headquarters in Riyadh, rather than anywhere else?

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:29.240
Is their fear of being denied government contracts, starting in 2024, the only driver of their decisions?

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:34.720
This question takes us to the second aspect of the Saudi plan, which is the soft or easy side, i.e. the carrot.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:39.400
Here we are talking about the incentives and facilities that the Saudi government provides to

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:43.840
international companies to persuade them to be present in the Saudi market.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.680
These incentives include, for example:

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:53.207
Long-term tax exemption for large companies / zero taxes for 50 years / preferential treatment in government contracts,

00:15:53.207 --> 00:15:59.000
and great facilities in terms of visa and sponsorship procedures for foreign employees and their families.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:05.200
For example, among the things that bothered foreign employees who work in international companies operating in Saudi Arabia,

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:10.520
is that in order to go out to spend the weekend in Dubai or Bahrain, they must obtain an exit visa.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:17.400
This issue is supposed to be addressed. There is also an exemption for a period of 10 years from the "Saudisation" policy,

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:21.320
which obliges companies to have a specified percentage of their employees Saudis.

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:26.720
Among the incentives is that the wives and husbands of foreign male and female employees

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:32.640
will be able to work in the country and obtain work permits. And their adult children, if they are over the legal age,

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:38.240
can live with their parents, and at the same time they will receive an education suitable for them in the city.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:45.440
In April 2021, the Royal Commission for Riyadh City announced that it had signed a partnership with the British King's College

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:51.160
School to open the first international school in Riyadh, which they named King's College Riyadh.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:57.000
In July of the same year, the Ministry of Investment and the Royal Commission for Riyadh City signed

00:16:57.000 --> 00:17:01.880
a partnership with the Spanish group (SEK) to open its first international school in the capital as well.

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:05.880
This is only a part of the carrot, there is another part related to infrastructure..

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:11.240
Riyadh is close to completing a $27 billion transportation network in the city.

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:15.560
The most important part of this network is the Riyadh Metro, which consists of 6 lines.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:20.720
In this context, it is also necessary to talk about the King Abdullah Financial District (KAFD),

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:27.840
as there is a plan to transform it into a special economic zone, exempt from entry visas and directly linked to Riyadh Airport.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:34.040
This center, built in the north of Riyadh on an area of ​​approximately 1.6 million square meters

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:40.400
and which includes about 59 skyscrapers, will provide one million cubic meters of office space

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:44.120
and can be considered a cornerstone of Saudi Arabia's plan

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:48.840
to lure as many regional centers of international companies as possible in the region.

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:53.080
In addition, there are plans to establish a number of special economic zones in the city. 

00:17:53.080 --> 00:18:00.360
In late October, Saudi Arabia inaugurated the Special Logistics Zone on an area of ​​3 million square kilometers.

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:05.360
It is the first free zone in the Kingdom and is located within the territory of King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:09.320
According to the statements of the Saudi Minister of Transport and Logistics, "Saleh Al-Jasser",

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:12.880
the American company Apple is one of the first companies

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:17.880
that leased a place within this free zone to use it as a regional distribution center.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:22.400
In total, Saudi Arabia announced that it intends to spend $220 billion

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:27.480
on developing Riyadh only in order to turn it into a global city by 2030.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:34.400
Apart from this, Saudi Arabia in general has lots of qualifications that make it attractive for multinational companies.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:40.000
More than 35 million people live there, making it the largest market in the Gulf region.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:45.200
However, it has large areas of land, cheap energy, ports on the Red Sea,

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:50.400
and a huge petrochemical industry that can provide many production inputs for manufacturers.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:57.200
All of the above are, in short, the most prominent tools that Saudi Arabia will use in its quest to be the largest host

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.880
for the regional centers of international companies in the region.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:05.200
Saudi Arabia has been already into talks with about 7,000 companies worldwide

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:08.320
to lure them to open their regional centers in Riyadh.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:15.360
It also aims, within 10 years, to lure the regional headquarters of about 480 international companies.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:20.200
This is a pretty large number considering that Dubai, which is the most important financial city in the region,

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.120
does not have half as many regional centers.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:27.160
According to a piece of information mentioned by the French News Agency in April 2021,

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:31.280
Dubai hosts about 140 regional headquarters of global companies.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:34.040
This is the highest number in the region and most importantly,

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:39.800
Dubai has reached this number of regional headquarters over the course of 3 decades.

00:19:39.800 --> 00:19:45.000
Therefore, some may see the Saudi plan as too optimistic, and others may see it as an exaggeration.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:50.160
However, the Saudis see it as ambitious and commensurate with the size and significance of the Kingdom's economy

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:54.640
as the only country in the region to be part of the global G-20 group.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:58.920
For us more important than ambition, optimism and pessimism is reality

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:02.640
- i.e. - apart from plans, declarations, optimism and pessimism, what is actually happening on the ground?

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:11.040
Last April, fDi Markets, issued by the Financial Times, said that by tracking the destination of 126 greenfield projects

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:15.120
that were revealed in Saudi Arabia during 2021,

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:22.360
55 of the projects are in Riyadh, and 14 of them were new regional centers.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:26.760
Of course, some of you might see this number is pretty small, but on the contrary, this number is considerable.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:34.040
It is worthy mentioning that from 2003 until the end of 2020, the main regional headquarters of foreign companies

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:43.240
that were established in Riyadh have not exceeded 11 centers. Now we are talking about 14 in just one year, which is 2021.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:49.720
The remarkable thing is that the headquarters that have been or will be inaugurated in the future in Riyadh

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.520
are not all new headquarters set up for the first time in the region.

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:56.200
On the contrary, some of them were previously in Dubai and moved to Riyadh.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:21:03.360
At the beginning of 2021, for example, the American company CSG decided to move its regional centers from Dubai to Riyadh.

00:21:03.360 --> 00:21:06.040
The headquarters, as a matter of fact, were moved from the Emirates to Saudi Arabia,

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:08.000
and work began within two months only.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:14.160
An incident like this shows that the rise and success of Riyadh will certainly and undoubtedly affect Dubai,

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:18.520
in short, there will be a strong and sought after competition between the two cities.

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:25.000
Official statements on the Saudi and Emirati sides downplay the competition too diplomatically.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:30.440
What is said on the Saudi side is that Riyadh's ambition does not target either Dubai or Abu Dhabi,

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:34.160
and it is ultimately okay if Riyadh is going to be like Singapore and Hong Kong. On the other hand,

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:39.080
the Emiratis also see that competition is in the interest of the region. This is the diplomatic talk,

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:44.520
on the ground nevertheless, every city is fighting over its current or future leading position and role.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:49.720
Dubai is very concerned in maintaining its current position as a significant financial and commercial center in the region,

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:58.960
so it has recently taken steps to ensure keeping that position. For example, in late June, Dubai announced a project called

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:08.520
"Dubai Global", which is a global network of 50 offices spread over five continents whose mission is marketing the city of Dubai

00:22:08.520 --> 00:22:15.600
and creating opportunities for Dubai-based companies in 30 new markets around the world.

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:18.986
It is necessary to draw attention quickly to a matter of significance,

00:22:18.986 --> 00:22:23.680
at the present time there are many things that distinguish Dubai from any other city in the region.

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:28.120
However, the two most significant features are: first, its ease for business inauguration.

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:37.200
Meaning, in 2020 the UAE in general ranked 16th globally and first in the Arab world in the ease of doing business index.

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:44.400
Saudi Arabia ranked 63rd, and that is an issue that Saudi Arabia is supposed to be addressing at the moment.

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:52.680
Second, the status of social openness in Dubai for international companies and their employees and foreign nationals in general,

00:22:52.680 --> 00:22:56.200
which in their view is higher than its peer in Riyadh.

00:22:56.200 --> 00:23:01.680
Meaning, the lifestyle and mores in Dubai, which is commensurate with being a global city,

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:08.480
is more comfortable for foreign officials and employees, most of whom are from countries whose lifestyle is open.

00:23:08.480 --> 00:23:13.040
This is one of the reasons why the entertainment authority in Saudi Arabia has been trying for many months

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:16.160
to make Riyadh keep pace with Dubai on this point.

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:21.760
A crucial question popped up here: Why are we, as countries, supposed to compete to lure the largest possible number

00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:26.280
of regional headquarters of giant international companies? What do we gain?

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:27.800
Yet, before answering such a question,

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:32.520
let's first explain what does it mean to have regional headquarters of an international company.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:33.320
Attention please…

00:23:33.320 --> 00:23:39.920
The first time that the concept of the Regional Head Quarter appeared was in the early sixties,

00:23:39.920 --> 00:23:44.920
during that period, American companies were expanding in Europe

00:23:44.920 --> 00:23:50.160
having activities and operations in European countries such as France, Germany and Britain.

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:55.920
With the amplification of business , American companies sought after an effective administration

00:23:55.920 --> 00:23:59.680
in the old continent to manage its operations there efficiently.

00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:06.800
Hence the idea of ​​a regional headquarters located in a country other than that of the parent company.

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:11.440
This headquarters is where part of the parent company's Chief Executive Officer is located,

00:24:11.440 --> 00:24:15.040
and through it, the company's operations are managed at the regional level.

00:24:15.040 --> 00:24:21.280
Among the first companies to do this were IBM when it opened a regional headquarters in Paris,

00:24:21.280 --> 00:24:26.800
and Ford Motors when it opened one in London. That's simply the idea of a regional headquarters.

00:24:26.800 --> 00:24:32.560
The Saudi government, within the framework of its regional headquarters program known as 'Programme HQ',

00:24:32.560 --> 00:24:38.760
has set a specific definition for the regional headquarters, which is: “A unit of a multinational group

00:24:38.760 --> 00:24:43.880
established under Saudi regulations for the purpose of supporting, managing

00:24:43.880 --> 00:24:47.200
and providing strategic direction for its branches and subsidiaries operating in the Middle East and North Africa.”

00:24:47.200 --> 00:24:55.000
Well, we know what a corporate headquarters means. But why would we want so many of them?

00:24:55.000 --> 00:24:57.560
What is the point of that? I will tell you a quick anecdote of significance.

00:24:57.560 --> 00:25:05.440
On September 7, 2017, the American e-commerce giant, "Amazon", announced its intention to open a new regional

00:25:05.440 --> 00:25:14.160
headquarters in North America. So, for any city in North America that would like to have the new company headquarter on its land,

00:25:14.160 --> 00:25:22.640
It has had to submit a file explaining why Amazon should choose it to set up the new headquarters.

00:25:22.640 --> 00:25:26.200
Each city should explain exactly what advantages it will be offering…

00:25:26.200 --> 00:25:31.320
Application closed on October 19, 2017, took about a month and a half.

00:25:31.320 --> 00:25:36.560
Guess how many North American cities have submitted their bid to Amazon

00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:40.760
and expressed interest in hosting the company's new regional headquarters?

00:25:40.760 --> 00:25:46.680
Do you think it's 10 cities? 20 cities? 50 cities? Did any of you think of the number 100?

00:25:46.680 --> 00:25:56.160
All of you probably got it wrong. On October 23 of the same year, Amazon declared that 238 cities in North America

00:25:56.160 --> 00:26:01.400
had submitted bids to lure it to set up its new headquarters on its land.

00:26:01.400 --> 00:26:04.160
Of course, it makes you wonder why all these cities did so? Will Amazon distribute money to the people and the local administration of the chosen city?

00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:12.840
Actually, opposite of what you expected, the answer is yes. Amazon will distribute money.

00:26:12.840 --> 00:26:20.400
This horrific turnout to participate in bidding for Amazon was a lust by these cities to the huge gains that will be achieved

00:26:20.400 --> 00:26:25.560
if Amazon sets up its new regional headquarters known as [Amazon HQ2] on their land.

00:26:25.560 --> 00:26:32.640
Amazon was planning to invest $5 billion in the new headquarters. It will directly employ 50,000 people.

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:38.000
Three times this number will be indirect labor, ie "150 thousand".

00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:41.440
Let us now from Amazon .. Of course you know Switzerland? Famous for chocolate and watches?

00:26:41.440 --> 00:26:46.280
About 25,500 multinational companies operate in that country.

00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:54.320
They constitute only about 5% of the total companies in it, which is 580,000 companies.

00:26:54.320 --> 00:27:02.680
Multinational corporations employ approximately 25-30% of the country's workforce,

00:27:02.680 --> 00:27:09.680
which is directly equivalent to 1.3 million people. However, it is responsible for one-third of the gross domestic product,

00:27:09.680 --> 00:27:12.560
and one-third of the tax revenues that enter the state treasury.

00:27:12.560 --> 00:27:17.640
This is the type of major economic benefits that Riyadh and Dubai are competing for.

00:27:17.640 --> 00:27:21.600
The Saudi government hopes that the regional headquarters program

00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:31.560
will add to the Saudi economy by 2030 about 67 billion riyals, or 18 billion dollars, and create about 30,000 jobs.

00:27:31.560 --> 00:27:36.640
Riyadh, to achieve this, will enter, as we said, in direct competition with Dubai.

00:27:36.640 --> 00:27:42.960
It will not be an easy competition at all, given that Dubai has made great strides in all directions,

00:27:42.960 --> 00:27:47.280
which has contributed to becoming one of the most important financial and business centers in the world.

00:27:47.280 --> 00:27:52.000
The competition could also be a triple after the 2022 World Cup,

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:55.920
an event that will present Qatar, and Doha in particular, to the whole world as well.

00:27:55.920 --> 00:28:02.240
Last March, the giant German car company "Volkswagen" established its regional headquarters for the Middle East

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:07.240
in the Qatari capital, Doha. Before Volkswagen, large companies such as Google and Microsoft

00:28:07.240 --> 00:28:09.920
began running their regional activities from Qatar.

00:28:09.920 --> 00:28:15.720
Last August, the Foreign Direct Investment Markets Bulletin / fDi Markets /

00:28:15.720 --> 00:28:23.600
said that Qatar attracted 71% of all investments in the Middle East during the second quarter of 2022.

00:28:23.600 --> 00:28:32.880
This contributed to the creation of 6,680 job opportunities in 11 projects, With investments amounting to 19.2 billion US dollars.

00:28:32.880 --> 00:28:39.760
In the end, I would like to say that the Middle East and North Africa region can accommodate four, five and six

00:28:39.760 --> 00:28:45.360
financial centers at the same time, given that it has huge untapped potential.

00:28:45.360 --> 00:28:51.200
In the 1970s, Hong Kong emerged as the first and largest financial center in the Asia Pacific region.

00:28:51.200 --> 00:28:57.040
Years later, Singapore and Shanghai competed with it for its position as the financial center of the region.

00:28:57.040 --> 00:29:06.520
Today, after decades of competition, the three cities not only became financial centers, but also rank among the top 10

00:29:06.520 --> 00:29:10.840
all over the world. Singapore is the third, Hong Kong fourth, and Shanghai sixth.

00:29:10.840 --> 00:29:16.600
We hope to see Riyadh, Cairo, Doha, Abu Dhabi, Casablanca and other major Arab capitals

00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:20.040
among the most important financial centers in the world, next to Dubai,

00:29:20.040 --> 00:29:27.080
which leads the scene as a financial center on the regional level, and in an advanced position on the global level.

00:29:27.080 --> 00:29:31.360
All the best to the Saudi siblings in their ambitious plans, wishing the same for the rest of the Arab cities.

00:29:31.360 --> 00:29:34.520
I am done here, and in the end I have a question for you guys:

00:29:34.520 --> 00:29:39.040
if you would choose an Arab city to live or settle in for a potential prosperous future, which city would you choose?

00:29:39.040 --> 00:29:47.800
I will follow all your answers in the comments, and I hope if you like the episode, like the video,

00:29:47.800 --> 00:29:52.000
share it with your friends and loved ones, and tell them about us, they may take advantage of it

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:57.000
- and above all - subscribe to the channel as we said, Good Bye...

